# The I/L's third class node: a spirit summoned for thirty seconds that brings
# down El Nath's blizzard every three seconds, twelve times on ten enemies.
#
# A buff with a pulse instead of its own summon, which is what a summon on a
# cooldown is here: Elquines and Thunder Sphere are permanent and need no
# duration, and this one is up a quarter of its cooldown. Darkness Aura has the
# same shape.
#
# Three seconds is GMS's `x`, the one number in its common block the tooltip
# never uses. The animation can't decide it (attack1 runs 810ms, and Phoenix's
# 1170ms animation ships at 1.71s, so animations have never set a summon's
# timing here), but the balance range can: ten pulses is 205,800% on a 120s
# cooldown, 1,715%/s against Bolt Barrage's 2,580%/s, while the 810ms reading
# would be 761,460%, far outside the range.
#
# Ten enemies is GMS's own. The rule gives 51 from the spirit's 1200x700 box,
# and it only lowers a cap, never raises one.
#
# GMS gives 3 Freeze Stacks "when attacking 1 enemy" and the usual 1 on a crowd.
# That is a bossing bonus written into the skill, not something ice does, so the
# skill states both instead of the one stack per line the element would give.
name: "Spirit of Snow"
description:
  "Summon the devastating frosts of the El Nath Mountains. They freeze what "
  "they touch."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ACTIVE
tags: SKILL_TAG_ICE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_ICE_LIGHTNING_ARCH_MAGE_V skill_order: 3 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
base_delay_ms: 120
cooldown_seconds: 120.0
freeze_seconds: 8.0
freeze_build {
  alone: 3
  crowd: 1
}
buff {
  duration_seconds: 30.0
  pulse {
    label: "Blizzard"
    cast_interval_seconds: 3.0
    lines: 12
    max_enemies: 10
    base { skill_pct: 8.16 }
    per_level { skill_pct: 0.31 }
  }
}
